cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Fulgurite: a disassembler and decompiler whose guesses are visible, explainable and reversible"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "MD Naved Raja"
    family-names: "Khan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0426-2822"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Naved124/fulgurite"
url: "https://navedkhan.dev/"
abstract: >-
  A reverse-engineering tool for x86-64 and AArch64 ELF and PE binaries that
  attaches a calibrated confidence and its evidence to every claim it makes,
  can explain any result, and lets the user reject an inference so it stays
  rejected. It includes hardened ELF and PE loaders, an x86 decoder, an
  AArch64 decoder generated from Arm's machine-readable specification, a fact
  store with confidence and evidence, function and control-flow recovery, and
  cross-references, checked against readelf, objdump and llvm-mc oracles, and
  a scorer that compares its function recovery with existing disassemblers.
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - disassembler
  - decompiler
  - binary analysis
  - function recovery
  - elf
  - pe
  - x86-64
  - aarch64
license: Apache-2.0
